Make the windowing feature selectable on the stable channel.

The editor shell builds its main window and floating panels on the windowing
API. That API and its macOS embedder support both ship in stable, but
flutter_tools declares the feature available on master only, so
`flutter config --enable-windowing` is a silent no-op there and the editor
exits at startup. The channel check in FlutterFeatureFlags.isEnabled runs
before environmentOverride, so FLUTTER_WINDOWING cannot reach it either, and
the tool rejects a hand-passed FLUTTER_ENABLED_FEATURE_FLAGS dart-define.

Applied to the revision in flutter.version, which is the only revision it is
known to apply to. Drop it once windowing reaches stable upstream
(flutter/flutter#30701).

diff --git a/packages/flutter_tools/lib/src/features.dart b/packages/flutter_tools/lib/src/features.dart
index c32c961972d..c9756340d8e 100644
--- a/packages/flutter_tools/lib/src/features.dart
+++ b/packages/flutter_tools/lib/src/features.dart
@@ -260,6 +260,7 @@ const windowingFeature = Feature(
   environmentOverride: 'FLUTTER_WINDOWING',
   runtimeId: 'windowing',
   master: FeatureChannelSetting(available: true),
+  stable: FeatureChannelSetting(available: true),
 );
 
